dom, “red”, was also given to him from his conduct in connection with the red lentil “pottage” for which he sold his birthright (30, 31).","verses":151,"father":"Isaac","mother":"Rebekah","v":[19]}],"places":[{"id":"jerusalem_636","name":"Jerusalem","kind":"City","lat":31.77667,"lon":35.23417,"summary":"Called also Salem, Ariel, Jebus, the “city of God,” the “holy city;” by the modern Arabs el-Khuds, meaning “the holy;” once “the city of Judah” (2 Chr. 25:28).","verses":754,"v":[1,6,16,17,20]},{"id":"valley_of_jehoshaphat_1209","name":"valley of Jehoshaphat","kind":"Valley","lat":31.77213,"lon":35.2366,"summary":"","verses":2,"v":[2,12]},{"id":"sidon_1093","name":"Sidon","kind":"City","lat":33.56024,"lon":35.37121,"summary":"A fishery, a town on the Mediterranean coast, about 25 miles north of Tyre. It received its name from the “first-born” of Canaan, the grandson of Noah (Gen. 10:15, 19).","verses":30,"v":[4]},{"id":"tyre_1184","name":"Tyre","kind":"City","lat":33.26807,"lon":35.20936,"summary":"A rock, now es-Sur; an ancient Phoenician city, about 23 miles, in a direct line, north of Acre, and 20 south of Sidon. Sidon was the oldest Phoenician city, but Tyre had a longer and more illustrious history.","verses":52,"v":[4]},{"id":"zion_1263","name":"Zion","kind":"Mountain","lat":31.77667,"lon":35.23417,"summary":"Sunny; height, one of the eminences on which Jerusalem was built. It was surrounded on all sides, except the north, by deep valleys, that of the Tyropoeon separating it from Moriah, which it surpasses in height by 105 feet.","verses":140,"v":[16,17,21]},{"id":"valley_of_shittim_1217","name":"valley of Shittim","kind":"Valley","lat":31.85826,"lon":35.64157,"summary":"","verses":1,"v":[18]},{"id":"edom_357","name":"Edom","kind":"Region","lat":31.25,"lon":34.75,"summary":"Idumea (Isa. 34:5, 6; Ezek. 35:15). “The field of Edom” (Gen. 32:3), “the land of Edom” (Gen. 36:16), was mountainous (Obad. 1:8, 9, 19, 21).","verses":79,"v":[19]},{"id":"egypt_362","name":